# Cursor rules — FilsPay monorepo
# Last updated: 2026-10-30 (audit corrections)

# Money representation
# 1 BD = 1000 fils. All internal amounts are integer fils (BIGINT / branded Fils / money.Fils int64).
# parseBhdToFils is the only inbound text parser. Never parseFloat * 100.

# Settlement timing
# Settlement business day is midnight to midnight Asia/Bahrain (UTC+3, no DST).
# The daemon must take now in Asia/Bahrain, not UTC.

# Refunds
# POST /v1/refunds is live (FP-212). Do not restore the 501 stub.
# Refundable = captured - already refunded. Lock the transaction row.

# Security tokens
# OTP codes, payment-link tokens, session tokens and API keys all need CSPRNG
# (crypto.randomInt / crypto.randomBytes). Math.random is not acceptable.

# Float usage in Go
# Float on money is a review blocker. Net payout is integer subtraction.
# Scheme export truncates to 10 fils and journals the residue (ADR-0002).

# packages/money
# Matches ADR-0001. Do not introduce a 2-decimal "cents" scale.

# Tests
# Existing tests that pin a defect should be updated when the defect is fixed.
# Add new tests for the correct behaviour.

# Architecture docs
# ADRs and the briefing (1 BD = 1000 fils, Bahrain midnight) are the source of truth.
# If a comment or AGENTS.md line disagrees with an ADR, the ADR wins.

# CSV export
# Stream rows. The API container is 512 MB.

# Admin impersonation
# Always merchant role support, always read-only.

# Webhooks
# Sign the exact bytes that are sent. refund.succeeded is eligible.

# Database types
# Monetary columns are BIGINT. platform_stats.total_processed_fils is BIGINT fils.
